  <datafield tag="590" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Forms part of: Brown, Jean, 1911-1994. Jean Brown papers, 1815-1995 (bulk 1916-1985). (Special Collections, accn. no. 890164).</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">In a portfolio shaped like a 2-dimensional bowler hat, inside a plastic bag.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Small works of Spoerri, Köpcke, Metzger, Page, Williams, Ben and me, Filliou, were presented by the Galerie Légitime, under the title The Frozen Exhibition, Oct. 23, 1962-Oct. 22, 1972. The Galerie Legitime (English version) consisted of a bowler hat ... The bowler hat containing the artworks was put inside a freezer bag - to underline that the exhibition would not only last for weeks, but for a full 10 years, at the end of which time the bag would be opened and the artworks defrosted ... The group show that was the occasion for the Frozen Exhibition [was] The Misfits' Fair (mistakingly called "Festival" on the invitations) ... [at] Gallery One, 16 North Audley Street, Grosvenor Square, London"--Container verso.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The Frozen Exhibition was frozen after its 1962 exhibition in London and subsequently lost. Then in 1972 a new version was issued as a multiple by VICE-Verlag in an ed. of 170 (cf. Robert Filliou 1926-1987).</subfield>
  </datafield>
